inclusion_criteria_en:
1. 18 years of age ≥ age ≤ 80 years;
2. Meet the diagnostic criteria of Western medicine PPPD and traditional Chinese medicine;
3. Be able to cooperate to complete the DHI scale, HAMA scale, and HAMD scale;
4. All patients voluntarily participate in the study and sign the informed consent form.

exclusion_criteria_en:
1. Primary psychiatric patients and patients with needle phobia;  
2. Individuals with a history of long-term alcohol abuse, substance dependence, suicidal tendencies, or cognitive decline;  
3. Exclusion of individuals with severe diseases of the heart, brain, liver, or kidneys;  
4. Exclusion of central vertigo, vestibular neuritis, Meniere's disease, or dizziness caused by other reasons.

study_objectives_en:
1. Through centralized monitoring of a large sample population, safety risk signals are identified. By interpreting and further evaluating the correlation between drugs and events, the causal relationship between the adverse event and the drug is clarified, providing a basis for safe clinical medication;
2. Discovering adverse reactions that did not occur before market launch, discovering suspicious and unexpected serious adverse reactions (SUSAR), and further evaluating to identify "unknown" (unconfirmed or unidentified) or insufficiently understood drug adverse reactions that were not discovered during the pre-market stage;
3. Clarify the incidence, manifestations, types, severity, and outcomes of adverse reactions of Guipi mixture, describe the spectrum of adverse reactions, quantify the risk of such adverse reactions in the population receiving drug treatment, and provide evidence-based support for improving the instructions of Guipi mixture.

inclusion_criteria_en:
1. Age ≥ 4 years old, ≤ 80 years old, gender not limited;
2. Patients who meet the indications specified in the instructions for Guipi mixture or are deemed suitable for the use of Guipi mixture by clinical physicians based on the patient's condition, and for whom a prescription has been issued for the use of Guipi mixture;
3. Patients who voluntarily participate and sign informed consent forms;
4. Continuous medication for more than 14 days is considered as one case.

exclusion_criteria_en:
A history of stroke with large infarctions or intracranial hemorrhage as indicated by cranial MRI;
Major arterial sclerosis;
White matter lesions due to other causes (immune demyelinating metabolic toxic infectious hereditary etc.);
Dizziness caused by other conditions (e.g. peripheral vestibular disorders systemic disease–induced dizziness dizziness related to psychological factors etc.);
Medication-induced pregnancy-related or hereditary dizziness;
Severe cognitive impairment (MoCA < 10);
Use of anti-vertigo medications within the past two weeks;
Currently participating in other clinical trials;
Those who do not meet the diagnostic and inclusion criteria.

inclusion_criteria_en:
(1) Gender unlimited, aged between 18 and 80 years old;

(2) Meets the diagnostic criteria for persistent postural perceptual dizziness, as well as the diagnostic criteria for liver yang hyperactivity syndrome in vertigo;

(3) Those who voluntarily participate in this experiment and sign an informed consent form;

(4) Having a certain level of education, able to read simple articles and write simple sentences in the past;

(5) No severe functional organs or other serious diseases are present.

exclusion_criteria_en:
(1) Individuals with dizziness/dizziness disorders other than Persistent postural perceptual dizziness;

(2) Has received or is currently taking anti anxiety/depression medication treatment within the past three months and has an impact on the observed indicators;

(3) Patients with other serious internal and external diseases;

(4) Patients with allergies or contraindications to the investigational drug;

(5) Researchers believe that they are unable to participate in the study due to other reasons;

(6) Unable to sign informed consent;

(7) Individuals with severe anxiety and depression.

inclusion_criteria_en:
(1) Meet diagnostic criteria for vestibular migraine with recent frequent episodes;
(2) Aged between 18 and 65 years (inclusive), any gender;
(3) Voluntary participation with good compliance, cooperative in examinations, and signed informed consent;

exclusion_criteria_en:
(1) Vestibular migraine overlapping with other vestibular disorders (e.g., Ménière's disease, Benign Paroxysmal Positional Vertigo, vestibular paroxysmia) or brainstem aura migraine/posterior circulation ischemia;
(2) Central nervous system disorders (e.g., cerebral infarction, hemorrhage, space-occupying lesions) excluded by MRI;
(3) Long-term use of analgesics, antivertigo drugs, antihistamines, or anxiolytics;
(4) Severe cervical spondylosis, cardiopulmonary/hepatic/renal diseases, or psychiatric disorders;
(5) Severe anxiety/depression;
(6) Pregnant or lactating women;
(7) Participation in other clinical trials within 3 months;
